            <ArticleTitle>ECG changes in hyperemesis gravidarum.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2016217158</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2016-217158</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This is a case report of a 30-year-old patient presenting at advanced gestation with hyperemesis, who developed a prolonged QT interval secondary to electrolyte imbalance during recovery. This potentially fatal complication should be considered in all patients with hyperemesis gravidarum, especially after a prolonged period of starvation. We hope to highlight the importance of ECG monitoring and careful prescribing in such cases, something that is not considered in current guidelines.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>2017 BMJ Publishing Group Ltd.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
